WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.510 --> 00:00:03.867
Why do humans return to Pandora in Avatar:
The Way of Water?

00:00:03.867 --> 00:00:05.938
Is it for more unobtanium?

00:00:05.938 --> 00:00:08.200
James Cameron might just surprise you!

00:00:08.592 --> 00:00:12.860
At its core, the "Avatar" franchise is an
outlandish science fiction fantasy.

00:00:12.860 --> 00:00:18.189
With its bizarre bevy of colorful creatures
and fantastical vistas, the world of Pandora

00:00:18.189 --> 00:00:23.910
undeniably embraces its strange concepts and
finds exciting ways to expand upon them continuously.

00:00:23.910 --> 00:00:28.590
However, the franchise's way of presenting
these larger-than-life ideas alongside its

00:00:28.590 --> 00:00:33.620
social commentary remains most intriguing,
even if it's far from the first sci-fi flick

00:00:33.620 --> 00:00:34.359
to do this.

00:00:34.359 --> 00:00:38.770
One of these attempts to connect the franchise's
wondrous settings to a real-world dilemma

00:00:38.770 --> 00:00:41.350
is with the special compound unobtanium.

00:00:41.350 --> 00:00:46.210
In the first "Avatar," we learn that Unobtanium
acts as a powerful superconductor, which those

00:00:46.210 --> 00:00:50.930
on Earth seek to use as a power source, given
the energy crisis they are experiencing.

00:00:50.930 --> 00:00:55.559
However, the Na'Vi people forbid the mining
of it, as they view the Tree of Souls, where

00:00:55.559 --> 00:00:57.629
it is located as a sacred place.

00:00:57.629 --> 00:01:01.870
The environmental metaphor may be pretty on
the nose, but it is nevertheless an integral

00:01:01.870 --> 00:01:07.020
part of the story "Avatar" tries to tell about
our inner connection with nature and how far

00:01:07.020 --> 00:01:08.225
we are willing to fight for it.

00:01:08.225 --> 00:01:11.591
"I am a warrior like you, i'm supposed to
fight"

00:01:11.591 --> 00:01:16.270
So it's all the more surprising that the film's
sequel, "Avatar: The Way of Water," never

00:01:16.270 --> 00:01:17.270
mentions Unobtanium.

00:01:17.270 --> 00:01:21.540
That's right, the very element that caused
the central conflict in Pandora's history

00:01:21.540 --> 00:01:24.220
is not given a single mention in "The Way
of Water."

00:01:24.220 --> 00:01:30.141
So what does the absence of this crucial substance
mean for the greater "Avatar" story moving forward?

00:01:30.141 --> 00:01:34.430
The term Unobtanium is not present in "Avatar:
The Way of Water," but that doesn't mean the

00:01:34.430 --> 00:01:36.759
idea behind the substance is lost.

00:01:36.759 --> 00:01:41.079
The film sees Colonel Miles Quaritch return
in an Avatar body to take down Jake Sully

00:01:41.079 --> 00:01:42.079
and his family.

00:01:42.079 --> 00:01:46.660
When Sully decides to move his family beyond
the outskirts of their forest home, they join

00:01:46.660 --> 00:01:49.969
the Metkayina tribe of the ocean, who teaches
the family their ways.

00:01:49.969 --> 00:01:54.420
Amongst the most crucial aspects of the Metakiyna
way of life comes their connection to the

00:01:54.420 --> 00:01:56.250
whale-like creatures, the Tulkuns.

00:01:56.250 --> 00:02:01.510
The people hold the intelligent creatures
in extremely high regard, seeing them as siblings

00:02:01.510 --> 00:02:05.100
and forming lifelong connections with the
animals from birth.

00:02:05.100 --> 00:02:08.810
In an attempt by Quaritch and his band of
goons to lure Sully from hiding, they team

00:02:08.810 --> 00:02:13.640
up with a ship of Tulkun hunters who help
kill the animals to cause distress to the

00:02:13.640 --> 00:02:14.640
Metakiyna clan.

00:02:14.640 --> 00:02:18.660
However, after killing the animals, the hunters
drill into their heads and take out a gloppy

00:02:18.660 --> 00:02:24.700
liquid that is incredibly valuable, with even
a small canister worth millions.

00:02:24.700 --> 00:02:29.239
In this way, the Tulkuns stand in as a similar
piece of symbolism that the Unobtanium did

00:02:29.239 --> 00:02:34.099
in the first film as a precious natural resource
that humanity seeks to exploit.

00:02:34.099 --> 00:02:38.209
It serves the message here, but even more
significantly, it paints a picture of what

00:02:38.209 --> 00:02:40.540
we can expect in the franchise's future.

00:02:40.540 --> 00:02:45.550
The seemingly forgotten Unobtanium might confuse
viewers coming into "Avatar: The Way of Water."

00:02:45.550 --> 00:02:49.950
As an essential plot point of the first film,
it seems natural that this long-awaited sequel

00:02:49.950 --> 00:02:55.010
finds new ways to expand and build upon what
we already know about the valuable substance.

00:02:55.010 --> 00:03:00.190
But just as "The Way of Water" explores new
and exciting lands in Pandora instead of staying

00:03:00.190 --> 00:03:04.650
in the same place as its predecessor, the
film chooses to evolve in its thematic nature

00:03:04.650 --> 00:03:05.150
as well.

00:03:08.439 --> 00:03:11.730
"This family is our fortress"
Keep in mind that "The Way of Water" takes

00:03:11.730 --> 00:03:15.180
place more than a decade after the first film's
events.

00:03:15.180 --> 00:03:19.980
In that time, the energy crisis on Earth has
likely taken over or, if not, is very close

00:03:19.980 --> 00:03:21.069
to doing so.

00:03:21.069 --> 00:03:24.290
Is Unobtanium still strong enough to solve
the issue?

00:03:24.290 --> 00:03:27.890
Even if it proves powerful, it's more than
likely that Colonel Quaritch and his gang

00:03:27.890 --> 00:03:32.730
will find similarly valuable resources throughout
Pandora and find some way to exploit them

00:03:32.730 --> 00:03:33.950
for their own use.

00:03:33.950 --> 00:03:38.819
The war against humanity is about more than
protecting the Na'vi people and the life on

00:03:38.819 --> 00:03:43.300
Pandora, but the heart and soul of the planet
itself that keeps everything in check.

00:03:43.300 --> 00:03:47.510
"The Way of Water" tells us that there is
no one little piece that matters as much as

00:03:47.510 --> 00:03:50.560
it is the entirety of the world that deserves
saving.

